{"id": "y0402", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Crabs live in a variety of environments, but they are most commonly found in saltwater. They thrive in marine bodies of water like the ocean and seas, where the salinity suits their physiology. Some species also adapt to estu aries or brackish waters near coast s, but generally, saltwater is their preferred habitat.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
