{"id": "y0522", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Jim decided to lose weight and chose exercise as his primary method. The reason he thought this would be effective is because, despite working out, you still have a basic need for food. Your body requires energy from eating, so even if you exercise regularly, you can ’t simply eliminate the need to eat altogether. Ex ercise helps burn calories, but it doesn ’t stop your body from needing nutrients, making diet control crucial. So the answer is A: need for food.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
