{"id": "y0546", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "When ice is in the sun, it will be melted. The heat from the sun causes the ice to absorb energy, which increases its temperature and turns it into liquid water. So the correct answer is B: melted.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
