{"id": "y1082", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The theory used as justification for US involvement in Vietnam was containment theory. This idea, developed during the Cold War, argued that communism should be stopped from spreading, so if any country fell to commun ism, it needed to be contain ed so it didn't spread further. That's why the U.S. supported South Vietnam against North Vietnam; they wanted to stop the spread of communism in Southeast Asia.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
